python -B -m ruff check core/pit_provenance.py core/pit_data.py core/alpaca_pit_backfill.py export_pit_prices.py build_pit_bundle.py verify_pit_bundle.py --no-cache
python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_pit_data.py tests/test_export_pit_prices.py
python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_task11_pit_transport_contract.py tests/test_task11_diagnostic_contract.py -k "bundle or transport or pit"
```

Results: compilation passed; Ruff reported `All checks passed!`; focused Task 1 pytest reported `30 passed, 1 skipped, 2 warnings in 0.70s`; precise schema-v1 compatibility selection reported `12 passed, 11 deselected, 2 warnings in 1.46s`.

The separate commit's pre-commit hooks passed Ruff, trailing-whitespace, end-of-files, YAML (no files), and merge-conflict checks. `git diff --check` passed before commit. The two warnings remain the known unsupported pytest `cache_dir` and third-party `websockets.legacy` deprecation warnings.

